    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4171" root="توأ" body-key="t">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَائِىٌّ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَاوِىٌّ</span> rel. ns. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَآءٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَا</span> the names
of the letter <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ت</span>; as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَيَوِىٌّ</span>: (TA ubi suprà:)
whence <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَصِيدَةٌ تَائِيَّةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَاوِيَّةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَيَوِيَّةٌ</span> (T, K,
TA, ubi suprà, [the last written in the CK
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَيْوِيَّةٌ</span>,] and the second is also mentioned in the S)
<i>A</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قصيدة</span> <i>of which the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَوِىّ</span>. <i>is</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ت</span> (TA ibid.)

